=== Prompt ===
Who is Mario from Nintendo?

=== Response ===
Mario is a beloved character in the world of Nintendo. He is the main protagonist in a series of popular video games created by the Japanese video game designer, Shigeru Miyamoto.

Mario was first introduced in the arcade game "Donkey Kong" in 1981. In this game, Mario (then known as "Jumpman") was a carpenter who had to rescue a damsel in distress named Pauline from the clutches of a giant ape named Donkey Kong.

However, it was in the 1985 game "Super Mario Bros." for the Nintendo Entertainment System (NES) that Mario became a household name. In this game, Mario had to navigate through a series of underground tunnels and pipes to rescue Princess Peach from the clutches of the evil Bowser.

Since then, Mario has become one of the most iconic characters in the world of gaming, appearing in numerous games, including platformers, racing games, sports games, and role-playing games. He is known for his red hat, blue overalls, and mustache, as well as his iconic jumping and power-up abilities.

Mario's success has spawned numerous spin-offs, including:

* Luigi, Mario's trusty brother
* Princess Peach, the ruler of the Mushroom Kingdom
* Bowser, the main antagonist
* Yoshi, a friendly dinosaur who helps Mario on his quests
* Toad, a mushroom-like character who assists Mario

The Mario franchise has sold over 330 million copies worldwide, making it one of the best-selling video game franchises of all time.

Overall, Mario is a beloved character who has become synonymous with Nintendo and the world of gaming. His iconic status and enduring popularity have cemented his place as one of the most recognizable characters in pop culture.

